<p>This policy describes {{ site.name }}, published by {{ site.legalName }}. It was last updated on October 23, 2026.</p>
<h2>Governing law</h2>
<p>This policy is issued by {{ site.legalName }}. It is governed by the laws of the State of Florida.</p>
<h2>What the site is</h2>
<p>The site is a set of static pages. It does not offer accounts, comments, or a message form that stores what you type. It does not sell personal information. It does not run an advertising network.</p>
<h2>Analytics</h2>
<p>Each HTML page loads a Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon from <code>https://static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js</code>. Cloudflare’s <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/analytics/web-analytics/about/">documentation</a> says the snippet collects page-view and visitor metrics with the browser Performance API, and that Web Analytics does not collect or use visitors’ personal data. That description is Cloudflare’s. This site does not add an advertising or social-tracking script of its own.</p>
<h2>Cookies</h2>
<p>This site’s pages do not set a separate advertising cookie. Your browser may still store ordinary technical data. Cloudflare’s beacon is described above. The host may use cookies or similar logs for its own service.</p>
<h2>Hosting</h2>
<p>The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub may process technical logs, such as IP address, user agent, and the page requested, to operate and secure the host. That processing is described in the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub General Privacy Statement</a>.</p>
<h2>Messages you send</h2>
<p>If you email the desk or open a repository issue, the message is used to reply, to correct a story, or to fix the site. Do not send passwords, payment card numbers, or other secrets in a story tip.</p>
<h2>Links</h2>
<p>Stories link to other sites, including company blogs and help centers. Those sites have their own policies and are not covered by this one.</p>
<h2>Children</h2>
<p>The site is not directed at children under 13, and it does not knowingly collect personal information from them.</p>
<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>When this policy changes, the date at the top of the page changes with it.</p>
<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>Privacy questions go to the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
